# Fork Command Router

When the user sends a **short command** (one line, few words, often without context), match it against the registry below **before** improvising. Then **read the linked skill or doc in full** and execute that workflow.

Matching: case-insensitive; aliases are OR — any alias is enough; allow minor typos and German/English mix.

## Command Registry

| Command ID | User says (aliases) | Do this immediately |
|------------|---------------------|---------------------|
| `artifact-sync` | `sync`, `sync smarttube`, `refresh artifact`, `update artifact`, `upstream sync`, `reload artifact`, `sync with upstream` | Read [`.cursor/skills/artifact-sync/SKILL.md`](../skills/artifact-sync/SKILL.md) and follow the full sync workflow (`./gradlew installApkArtifact`). |
| `artifact-status` | `artifact status`, `upstream status`, `base status`, `apk status`, `fork status` | Read artifact-sync skill. Report installed artifact status only — do **not** re-download unless the user asked to sync. |
| `milestone-status` | `milestone status`, `meilenstein status`, `milestone progress`, `meilenstein progress` | Resolve **current** milestone in `fork-docs/milestones/`: (1) user-named in this message/conversation, else (2) most recently modified `MILESTONE_*.md`. Read it; report progress table; state next open step. Do **not** implement unless asked. |
| `next-step` | `next step`, `was jetzt`, `continue milestone`, `nächster schritt` | Same current-milestone resolution as `milestone-status`. Apply [milestone-implementation-workflow.mdc](milestone-implementation-workflow.mdc): outline approach, wait for confirmation, then implement. |
| `log-change` | `log change`, `changelog`, `fork changelog`, `document change` | Update [`fork-docs/CHANGELOG.md`](../../fork-docs/CHANGELOG.md) per [changelog-fork.mdc](changelog-fork.mdc). |
| `git-commit` | `git commit`, `commit`, `commit changes`, `commit it` | Read [`.cursor/skills/fork-git/SKILL.md`](../skills/fork-git/SKILL.md). Analyze diff, **split into small logical Conventional Commits packages**, commit each (`PlexServiceCore` first if needed). Do not push. |
| `git-push` | `git push`, `push`, `push changes`, `push it` | Read fork-git skill. Push `PlexServiceCore` first if unpushed, then SmartTublex root. Never force-push. |
| `commit-push` | `commit push`, `commit and push`, `commit & push`, `ship`, `ship it` | Read fork-git skill. Full commit workflow, then push workflow. |
| `fork-help` | `fork help`, `fork commands`, `commands`, `hilfe fork` | Show compact list from [`fork-docs/COMMANDS.md`](../../fork-docs/COMMANDS.md). |

## Router Rules

1. **One command → one workflow.** Do not blend workflows unless the user combines commands in one message.
2. **Read before act.** For skill-backed commands, read the entire `SKILL.md` before running tools.
3. **German and English** aliases are equivalent.
4. **Ambiguous input:** If two commands match, ask once (max one question).
5. **New commands:** When adding a skill or recurring workflow, register it here and in `fork-docs/COMMANDS.md`.

## Adding New Commands

When creating a new project skill under `.cursor/skills/`:

1. Add a row to this registry with aliases.
2. Add a row to `fork-docs/COMMANDS.md`.
3. Put trigger terms in the skill's YAML `description` field.
